\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Pushforward rollout training with a horizon curriculum. The surrogate is unrolled autoregressively from a data state $\mathbf  {s}_t$; the first $K-g$ steps are executed without gradients (grey) and only the final $g=2$ steps carry gradients (orange). The MSE loss $\mathcal  {L}$ is applied at the terminal prediction $\hat  {\mathbf  {s}}_{t+K}$ against the data target $\mathbf  {s}_{t+K}$. A curriculum ramps the rollout horizon $K$ from $K_0$ to $K_{\max }$ over training, exposing the model to its own prediction errors without backpropagating through the full rollout graph.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pushforward}{{3}{5}{Pushforward rollout training with a horizon curriculum. The surrogate is unrolled autoregressively from a data state $\state _t$; the first $K-g$ steps are executed without gradients (grey) and only the final $g=2$ steps carry gradients (orange). The MSE loss $\mathcal {L}$ is applied at the terminal prediction $\shat _{t+K}$ against the data target $\state _{t+K}$. A curriculum ramps the rollout horizon $K$ from $\kzero $ to $\kmax $ over training, exposing the model to its own prediction errors without backpropagating through the full rollout graph.\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
